STEP 2 -- CREATE TWO VRFs AND MOVE ONE SVI INTO EACH  (tests G6, G7, G8)
------------------------------------------------------------
  Applied 23:25:07-23:25:24, tools/ckcon.py (NOT cfg.py -- `ip vrf forwarding` emits a `%`
  advisory mid-batch and cfg.py would abandon everything after it; the T43849 trap):

    awplus(config)# ip vrf red
    awplus(config-vrf)# exit
    awplus(config)# ip vrf blue
    awplus(config-vrf)# exit
    awplus(config)# interface vlan10
    awplus(config-if)# ip vrf forwarding red
    **% All IP addresses configured on interface vlan10 have been removed**
    awplus(config-if)# do show running-config interface vlan10
    !
    interface vlan10
     ip vrf forwarding red
    !                                   <- the address really is GONE, not merely hidden
    awplus(config-if)# ip address 192.168.10.1/24
    awplus(config-if)# exit
    awplus(config)# interface vlan48
    awplus(config-if)# ip vrf forwarding blue
    **% All IP addresses configured on interface vlan48 have been removed**
    awplus(config-if)# ip address 192.168.48.1/24

  ⇒ **G7 CONFIRMED, and the device says so explicitly.**  Moving an interface into a VRF
  unsets its IP configuration, and the `do show running-config interface vlan10` in the middle
  of the batch proves it in the configuration itself, not just in a message.  A script that
  moves an SVI into a VRF and does not re-apply the address silently loses the address.

  Read back (23:25:3x):
    awplus# show ip vrf
    Name                    Default RD            Interfaces
    red                     --                    lo1
                                                  vlan10
    blue                    --                    lo2
                                                  vlan48
  ⇒ **G8 CONFIRMED**: `lo1` and `lo2` were created automatically, one per VRF; neither was
    asked for.  Default RD is `--` (none configured), as expected without BGP route leaking.

    awplus# show ip route
    C       10.0.41.0/30 is directly connected, vlan41
    C       10.0.61.0/30 is directly connected, vlan61
    Gateway of last resort is not set
